addEdges -- creates a list of graphs obtained by adding one new edge to the given graph in all possible ways
************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Ll = addEdges L
        Lg = addEdges G
        Ls = addEdges S
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing graphs in various
        formats
      * S, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, which describes a graph in
        Graph6 or Sparse6 format
      * G, a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * MaxDegree => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null,
        the maximum degree allowable for any vertex in the output graphs
      * NoNew3Cycles => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false, whether graphs with new 3-cycles are allowed
      * NoNew4Cycles => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false, whether graphs with new 4-cycles are allowed
      * NoNew5Cycles => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false, whether graphs with new 5-cycles are allowed
      * NoNewOddCycles => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value false, whether graphs with new odd-cycles are allowed
      * NoNewSmallCycles => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value
        null, an upper bound on cycles which are not allowed
  * Outputs:
      * Ll, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the list of graphs obtained from
        the graphs in $L$ in Graph6 format
      * Lg, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the list of graphs obtained from
        $G$
      * Ls, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the list of strings (in Graph6
        format) obtained from $S$

Description
===========

Simply creates a list, in the same format as the input, of all possible graphs
obtained by adding one new edge to the input graph.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..e];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : addEdges cycle R                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {a, c}, {b, c}, {c, d}, {a, e}, {d, e}}},    |
|            "ring" => R                                                      |
|            "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                    |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}, {a, d}, {c, d}, {a, e}, {d, e}}},     |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}, {b, d}, {c, d}, {a, e}, {d, e}}},     |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}, {c, d}, {a, e}, {b, e}, {d, e}}},     |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}, {c, d}, {a, e}, {c, e}, {d, e}}}}     |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If the List input format is used, then one should use care as the list may
contain isomorphic pairs.

