File: Nauty.info, Node: areIsomorphic, Next: buildGraphFilter, Prev: addEdges, Up: Top

areIsomorphic -- determines whether two graphs are isomorphic
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        b = areIsomorphic(G, H)
        G == H
        b = areIsomorphic(S, T)
        b = areIsomorphic(S, H)
        S == H
        b = areIsomorphic(G, T)
        G == T
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, 
      * H, a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, 
      * S, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
      * T, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether the two
        graphs are isomorphic

Description
===========

A very efficient method for determining whether two graphs (of the same format)
are isomorphic.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..e];                                          |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : areIsomorphic(cycle R, graph {a*c, c*e, e*b, b*d, d*a})|
|                                                            |
|o2 = true                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : areIsomorphic(cycle R, completeGraph R)                |
|                                                            |
|o3 = false                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : cycle R == "Dhc"                                       |
|                                                            |
|o4 = true                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

