countGraphs -- counts the number of graphs in the list with given properties
****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        n = countGraphs(L, s)
        n = countGraphs(L, h)
        n = countGraphs(L, l)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing graphs (mixed formats
        are allowed)
      * s, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, a filter, as generated by
        *note buildGraphFilter: buildGraphFilter,
      * h, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, a filter, as used by
        *note buildGraphFilter: buildGraphFilter,
      * l, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a filter, as used by *note
        buildGraphFilter: buildGraphFilter,
  * Outputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of graphs in $L$
        satisfying the filter

Description
===========

Counts the number of graphs in a list that satisfy certain restraints as given
in the filter (see *note buildGraphFilter: buildGraphFilter,).  Notice that the
input list can be graphs represented as instances of the class *note Graph:
(EdgeIdeals)Graph, or in a nauty-based *note String: (Macaulay2Doc)String,
format.

For example, we can count the number of connected graphs on five vertices.

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = generateGraphs 5;                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : countGraphs(L, {"Connectivity" => 0, "NegateConnectivity" => true})|
|                                                                        |
|o2 = 21                                                                 |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note buildGraphFilter: buildGraphFilter, -- creates the appropriate filter
    string for use with filterGraphs and countGraphs
  * *note filterGraphs: filterGraphs, -- filters (i.e., selects) graphs in a
    list for given properties

