generateBipartiteGraphs -- generates the bipartite graphs with a given bipartition
**********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        G = generateBipartiteGraphs n
        G = generateBipartiteGraphs(n, m)
        G = generateBipartiteGraphs(n, m, e)
        G = generateBipartiteGraphs(n, m, le, ue)
        G = generateBipartiteGraphs R
        G = generateBipartiteGraphs(R, m)
        G = generateBipartiteGraphs(R, m, e)
        G = generateBipartiteGraphs(R, m, le, ue)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, the ring in
        which the graphs will be created
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of vertices of the
        graphs, must be positive (see caveat)
      * m, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of vertices in the
        first class of the bipartition
      * e, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of edges in the
        graphs
      * le, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a lower bound on the number of
        edges in the graphs
      * ue, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, an upper bound on the number
        of edges in the graphs
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Class2Degree2 => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false, whether the vertices in the second class must have at
        least two neighbors of degree at least 2
      * Class2DistinctNeighborhoods => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, whether all vertices in
        the second class must have distinct neighborhoods
      * Class2MaxCommonNeighbors => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,
        default value null, an upper bound on the number of common neighbors of
        vertices in the second class
      * MaxDegree => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null,
        an upper bound on the degrees of the vertices
      * MinDegree => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null, a
        lower bound on the degrees of the vertices
      * OnlyConnected => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false, whether to only allow connected graphs
  * Outputs:
      * G, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the bipartite graphs satisfying
        the input conditions

Description
===========

This method generates all bipartite graphs on $n$ vertices. The size of the
bipartition is specified by giving the size of one class; the other class is
determined automatically from the number of vertices.

If only one integer argument is given, then the method generates all bipartite
graphs on that number of vertices with first class of sizes $0$ to $n$.

If a PolynomialRing $R$ is supplied instead, then the number of vertices is the
number of generators.  Moreover, the strings are automatically converted to
graphs in $R$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..e];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : generateBipartiteGraphs(R, 2)                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {Graph{"edges" => {}                }, Graph{"edges" => {{a, e}}        |
|            "ring" => R                           "ring" => R                |
|            "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}         "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|       }, Graph{"edges" => {{a, e}, {b, e}}  }, Graph{"edges" => {{a, d}, {a,|
|                "ring" => R                           "ring" => R            |
|     e}         "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}         "vertices" => {a, b, c,|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     e}}  }, Graph{"edges" => {{a, d}, {b, e}}  },                           |
|                   "ring" => R                                               |
|     d, e}         "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                             |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Graph{"edges" => {{a, d}, {a, e}, {b, e}}},                             |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Graph{"edges" => {{a, d}, {b, d}, {a, e}, {b, e}}},                     |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Graph{"edges" => {{a, c}, {a, d}, {a, e}}},                             |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Graph{"edges" => {{a, c}, {a, d}, {a, e}, {b, e}}},                     |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Graph{"edges" => {{a, c}, {b, d}, {a, e}}},                             |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Graph{"edges" => {{a, c}, {b, d}, {a, e}, {b, e}}},                     |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Graph{"edges" => {{a, c}, {a, d}, {b, d}, {a, e}, {b, e}}},             |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Graph{"edges" => {{a, c}, {b, c}, {a, d}, {b, d}, {a, e}, {b, e}}}}     |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The number of vertices $n$ must be positive as nauty cannot handle graphs with
zero vertices.

See also
========

  * *note generateGraphs: generateGraphs, -- generates the graphs on a given
    number of vertices

