graphComplement -- computes the complement of a graph
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L' = graphComplement L
        T = graphComplement S
        H = graphComplement G
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing graphs in various
        formats
      * S, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, a graph encoded in either
        Sparse6 or Graph6 format
      * G, a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * OnlyIfSmaller => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false, when true, then the smaller (fewer edges) of the graph and
        its complement are returned
  * Outputs:
      * L', a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the graph complement of the
        elements of $L$ stored in Graph6 format
      * T, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, the graph complement of $S$
        stored in the same format at $S$
      * H, a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, the graph complement of $G$

Description
===========

This method computes the graph complement of the input graph and returns the
result in the same format.

For graphs as defined in the *note EdgeIdeals: (EdgeIdeals)Top, package, one
can use the *note complementGraph: (EdgeIdeals)complementGraph, method to
achieve the same effect; however, this method provides the option of not taking
the complement if the complement has more edges than the graph itself.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..e];                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : graphComplement cycle R                                   |
|                                                               |
|o2 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, c}, {a, d}, {b, d}, {b, e}, {c, e}}}|
|           "ring" => R                                         |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                       |
|                                                               |
|o2 : Graph                                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : graphComplement "Dhc"                                     |
|                                                               |
|o3 = DUW                                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

Batch calls can be performed considerably faster when using the List input
format.  However, care should be taken as the returned list is entirely in
Graph6 or Sparse6 format.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : G = generateBipartiteGraphs 7;                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : time graphComplement G;                               |
| -- used 0.000637059s (cpu); 0.000629616s (thread); 0s (gc)|
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : time (graphComplement \ G);                           |
| -- used 0.0648894s (cpu); 0.0628245s (thread); 0s (gc)    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note complementGraph: (EdgeIdeals)complementGraph, -- returns the
    complement of a graph or hypergraph

