graphToString -- converts a graph to a string in the Graph6 format
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        S = graphToString(E, n)
        S = graphToString I
        S = graphToString G
        S = graphToString T
  * Inputs:
      * E, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of edge pairs
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of vertices in the
        graph, must be positive (see caveat)
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the edge ideal of a graph
      * G, a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, 
      * T, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, a string containing a graph;
        the string automatically passes through untouched
  * Outputs:
      * S, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, the graph converted to a
        Graph6 format string

Description
===========

This method converts various ways of representing a graph into nauty's Graph6
string format.  Note that if the *note Ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal, (or *note
MonomialIdeal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,) passed to the method is not
squarefree and monomial, then the method may have unknown and possibly
undesired results.

In this example, all graphs are the 5-cycle.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : graphToString({{0,1}, {1,2}, {2,3}, {3,4}, {0,4}}, 5)|
|                                                          |
|o1 = Dhc                                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = QQ[a..e];                                        |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : graphToString monomialIdeal (a*c, a*d, b*d, b*e, c*e)|
|                                                          |
|o3 = DUW                                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : graphToString cycle R                                |
|                                                          |
|o4 = Dhc                                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : graphToString "Dhc"                                  |
|                                                          |
|o5 = Dhc                                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

We note that if the input is a string, then the output is simply that string
returned, regardless of format or correctness.

Caveat
======

Notice that if using a *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, and number of vertices
input to create the string, then the *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, must have
vertices labeled $0$ to $n-1$.

The number of vertices $n$ must be positive as nauty cannot handle graphs with
zero vertices.

See also
========

  * *note Comparison of Graph6 and Sparse6 formats: Comparison of Graph6 and
    Sparse6 formats,
  * *note graph6ToSparse6: graph6ToSparse6, -- converts a Graph6 string to a
    Sparse6 string
  * *note sparse6ToGraph6: sparse6ToGraph6, -- converts a Sparse6 string to a
    Graph6 string
  * *note stringToGraph: stringToGraph, -- converts a Sparse6 or Graph6 String
    to a Graph in the given polynomial ring

