isPlanar -- determines if a given graph is planar
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        p = isPlanar G
        p = isPlanar S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, a graph encoded in either
        Sparse6 or Graph6 format
      * G, a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * p, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether the given
        graph is planar

Description
===========

A graph is planar if the graph can be embedded in the plane, i.e., the vertices
can be arranged such that no edges cross except at vertices.

+-----------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..e];           |
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : isPlanar cycle R        |
|                             |
|o2 = true                    |
+-----------------------------+
|i3 : isPlanar completeGraph R|
|                             |
|o3 = false                   |
+-----------------------------+

This method uses the program planarg. The code was written by Paulette Lieby
for the Magma project and used with permission in the software nauty.

See also
========

  * *note onlyPlanar: onlyPlanar, -- removes non-planar graphs from a list

