relabelBipartite -- relabels a bipartite graph so all vertices of a given class are contiguous
**********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L' = relabelBipartite L
        T = relabelBipartite S
        H = relabelBipartite G
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of bipartite graphs in
        various formats
      * S, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, a bipartite graph encoded in
        either Sparse6 or Graph6 format
      * G, a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, a bipartite graph
  * Outputs:
      * L', a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of graphs isomorphic to
        $S$
      * T, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, a graph isomorphic to $S$
        encoded in either Sparse6 or Graph6 format
      * H, a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, a graph isomorphic to $G$

Description
===========

A bipartite graph can be labeled so all vertices of a given class are
contiguous.  This method does precisely that to a bipartite graph.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..f];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : G = graph flatten apply({a,c,e}, v->v*{b,d,f})                          |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}, {a, d}, {c, d}, {b, e}, {d, e}, {a,   |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e, f}                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Graph                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|f}, {c, f}, {e, f}}}                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : relabelBipartite G                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, d}, {b, d}, {c, d}, {a, e}, {b, e}, {c, e}, {a,   |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e, f}                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Graph                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|f}, {b, f}, {c, f}}}                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If any of the inputs are not bipartite graphs, then the method throws an error.

See also
========

  * *note relabelGraph: relabelGraph, -- applies a vertex invariant based
    refinement to a graph

Ways to use relabelBipartite:
=============================

  * "relabelBipartite(Graph)"
  * "relabelBipartite(List)"
  * "relabelBipartite(String)"

