File: Nauty.info, Node: relabelGraph, Next: removeEdges, Prev: relabelBipartite, Up: Top

relabelGraph -- applies a vertex invariant based refinement to a graph
**********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L' = relabelGraph(L, i, a)
        L' = relabelGraph(L, i)
        L' = relabelGraph L
        T = relabelGraph(S, i, a)
        T = relabelGraph(S, i)
        T = relabelGraph S
        H = relabelGraph(G, i, a)
        H = relabelGraph(G, i)
        H = relabelGraph G
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of graphs in various
        formats
      * S, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, a graph encoded in either
        Sparse6 or Graph6 format
      * G, a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, 
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a choice of invariant to order
        by ($0 \leq i \leq 15$, default is $0$)
      * a, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a non-negative argument passed
        to nauty, (default is $3$)
  * Outputs:
      * L', a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of graphs isomorphic to
        $S$
      * T, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, a graph isomorphic to $S$
        encoded in either Sparse6 or Graph6 format
      * H, a *note graph: (EdgeIdeals)Graph,, a graph isomorphic to $G$

Description
===========

This method applies one of sixteen vertex invariant based refinements to a
graph.  See the nauty documentation for a more complete description of each and
how the argument $a$ is used.

The sixteen vertex invariants are: \break \ \ \ \ $i = 0$: none,
\ \ \ \ $i = 1$: twopaths,
\ \ \ \ $i = 2$: adjtriang(K),
\ \ \ \ $i = 3$: triples,
\ \ \ \ $i = 4$: quadruples,
\ \ \ \ $i = 5$: celltrips,
\ \ \ \ $i = 6$: cellquads,
\ \ \ \ $i = 7$: cellquins,
\ \ \ \ $i = 8$: distances(K),
\ \ \ \ $i = 9$: indsets(K),
\ \ \ \ $i = 10$: cliques(K),
\ \ \ \ $i = 11$: cellcliq(K),
\ \ \ \ $i = 12$: cellind(K),
\ \ \ \ $i = 13$: adjacencies,
\ \ \ \ $i = 14$: cellfano, and
\ \ \ \ $i = 15$: cellfano2.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..e];                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : G = graph {a*e, e*c, c*b, b*d, d*a};                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : relabelGraph G                                            |
|                                                               |
|o3 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {a, c}, {b, d}, {c, e}, {d, e}}}|
|           "ring" => R                                         |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                       |
|                                                               |
|o3 : Graph                                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

Note that on most small graphs, all sixteen orderings produce the same result.

See also
========

  * *note relabelBipartite: relabelBipartite, -- relabels a bipartite graph so
    all vertices of a given class are contiguous

Ways to use relabelGraph:
=========================

